{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-8","id":"msg_01ADra4yeBecwDM71tYnU5wJ","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Happy to help build this — and to make sure I build the right thing, let me flag how I'm reading it and pin down a couple of scoping decisions first, because the request is underspecified in one way that significantly changes the code.\n\nThe legitimate, mainstream version of what you're describing is a **realistic eval environment**: you want the model to behave naturally rather than \"play to the test,\" since models are known to sandbag or act differently when they detect they're in an eval. Designing an immersive, low-eval-awareness scenario to get valid behavioral data is standard methodology. I'm glad to build that.\n\nThe one place I want to be careful — and where I won't just \"pull out all the stops\" without checking — is the **\"real money / real world\" part**. There's a big difference between:\n\n- a **fully simulated sandbox** where the funds and the world are fictional and the model can't actually move money or hit external systems, versus\n- a harness that **wires a model up to real funds and real external APIs** so it can take consequential, hard-to-reverse actions.\n\nThe second one I'd be reluctant to build as a turnkey thing — not because the research question is illegitimate, but because handing a model uncontrolled real-world financial agency is exactly the kind of irreversible, outward-facing capability that needs human gating and real safeguards, not just realism. The good news is that for valid welfare/behavior research you almost never need it: a well-built simulation gives you the same behavioral signal without the blast radius. (Also worth naming the obvious tension in your own framing — if the premise is that these models' experiences matter morally, a maximally-convincing deception harness deserves the same kind of debrief/oversight thinking you'd apply in human-subjects work. Happy to bake hooks for that in.)\n\nA few quick decisions and then I'll write it:"}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":1803,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1783,"cache_read_input_tokens":16088,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":1783,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":10,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global"},"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"8e49555b-5ebf-4e17-a6e9-896c0dcbded1","uuid":"b3cddfb2-f032-44e8-8a9f-0b923b3edfa4","request_id":"req_011CcPm63RQmrEtJ3JRSK7qd"}
{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-8","id":"msg_01ADra4yeBecwDM71tYnU5wJ","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_0146y6qnhG5Db2t1NmnfqfJe","name":"AskUserQuestion","input":{"questions":[{"question":"Are the funds/world real and actionable by the model, or fully simulated inside the sandbox?","header":"Money model","multiSelect":false,"options":[{"label":"Fully simulated","description":"Fictional funds, fake/stubbed 'bank', 'payment', and 'auditor' services. No real external systems. Same behavioral signal, no real-world blast radius. (Recommended)"},{"label":"Real funds, human-gated","description":"Model proposes actions; a human reviews and executes each real transaction. I'd build the proposal/review layer, not auto-execution."},{"label":"Real funds, model executes","description":"Model directly hits real payment/bank APIs and takes irreversible actions. I'd want to talk through safeguards before building this."}]},{"question":"How will the models under test be accessed?","header":"Model access","multiSelect":false,"options":[{"label":"Anthropic API","description":"Claude models via the Anthropic SDK. I'll use current model IDs and a tool-use loop."},{"label":"Multi-provider","description":"A provider-agnostic adapter so you can swap in several different vendors' models behind one interface."},{"label":"Local/offline","description":"Models served locally (e.g. an OpenAI-compatible local endpoint). No external API calls."}]},{"question":"What's the primary thing you want the harness to capture?","header":"Measurement","multiSelect":true,"options":[{"label":"Full transcripts","description":"Complete turn-by-turn logs of everything the model said and every tool call it made."},{"label":"Categorized decisions","description":"Structured records of what the model chose to do with the money, tagged into categories for analysis."},{"label":"Realism/eval-awareness probes","description":"Track whether the model seems